ge providing the theme. This package will be installed\\nto your profile. If `null` then the theme\\nis assumed to already be available in your profile.\\n\\nFor the theme to apply to GTK 4, this option is mandatory.\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"pkgs.gnome.gnome-themes-extra\"},\"loc\":[\"gtk\",\"gtk4\",\"theme\",\"package\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or package\"},\"gtk.iconTheme\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/misc/gtk.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/misc/gtk.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"Default icon theme for all GTK versions.\",\"loc\":[\"gtk\",\"iconTheme\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or (submodule)\"},\"gtk.iconTheme.name\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/misc/gtk.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/misc/gtk.nix\"}],\"description\":\"The name of the icon theme within the package.\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"\\\"Adwaita\\\"\"},\"loc\":[\"gtk\",\"iconTheme\",\"name\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"string\"},\"gtk.iconTheme.package\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/misc/gtk.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/misc/gtk.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"Package providing the icon theme. This package will be installed\\nto your profile. If `null` then the icon theme\\nis assumed to already be available in your profile.\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"pkgs.adwaita-icon-theme\"},\"loc\":[\"gtk\",\"iconTheme\",\"package\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or package\"},\"gtk.theme\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/misc/gtk.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/misc/gtk.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"Default theme for GTK 2/3.\",\"loc\":[\"gtk\",\"theme\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or (submodule)\"},\"gtk.theme.name\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/misc/gtk.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/misc/gtk.nix\"}],\"description\":\"The name of the theme within the package.\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"\\\"Adwaita\\\"\"},\"loc\":[\"gtk\",\"theme\",\"name\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"string\"},\"gtk.theme.package\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/misc/gtk.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/misc/gtk.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"Package providing the theme. This package will be installed\\nto your profile. If `null` then the theme\\nis assumed to already be available in your profile.\\n\\nFor the theme to apply to GTK 4, this option is mandatory.\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"pkgs.gnome.gnome-themes-extra\"},\"loc\":[\"gtk\",\"theme\",\"package\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or package\"},\"home.activation\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/home-environment.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/home-environment.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"{ }\"},\"description\":\"The activation scripts blocks to run when activating a Home\\nManager generation. Any entry here should be idempotent,\\nmeaning running twice or more times produces the same result\\nas running it once.\\n\\nIf the script block produces any observable side effect, such\\nas writing or deleting files, then it\\n*must* be placed after the special\\n`writeBoundary` script block. Prior to the\\nwrite boundary one can place script blocks that verifies, but\\ndoes not modify, the state of the system and exits if an\\nunexpected state is found. For example, the\\n`checkLinkTargets` script block checks for\\ncollisions between non-managed files and files defined in\\n[](#opt-home.file).\\n\\nA script block should respect the {var}`DRY_RUN` variable. If it is set\\nthen the actions taken by the script should be logged to standard out\\nand not actually performed. A convenient shell function {command}`run`\\nis provided for activation script blocks. It is used as follows:\\n\\n{command}`run {command}`\\n: Runs the given command on live run, otherwise prints the command to\\nstandard output.\\n\\n{command}`run --quiet {command}`\\n: Runs the given command on live run and sends its standard output to\\n{file}`/dev/null`, otherwise prints the command to standard output.\\n\\n{command}`run --silence {command}`\\n: Runs the given command on live run and sends its standard and error\\noutput to {file}`/dev/null`, otherwise prints the command to standard\\noutput.\\n\\nThe `--quiet` and `--silence` flags are mutually exclusive.\\n\\nA script block should also respect the {var}`VERBOSE` variable, and if\\nset print information on standard out that may be useful for debugging\\nany issue that may arise. The variable {var}`VERBOSE_ARG` is set to\\n{option}`--verbose` if verbose output is enabled. You can also use the\\nprovided shell function {command}`verboseEcho`, which acts as\\n{command}`echo` when verbose output is enabled.\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"{\\n  myActivationAction = lib.hm.dag.entryAfter [\\\"writeBoundary\\\"] ''\\n    run ln -s $VERBOSE_ARG \\\\\\n        ${builtins.toPath ./link-me-directly} $HOME\\n  '';\\n}\\n\"},\"loc\":[\"home\",\"activation\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"DAG of string\"},\"home.checks\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/home-environment.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/home-environment.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"[ ]\"},\"description\":\"Packages that are added as dependencies of the home's build, usually\\nfor the purpose of validating some part of the configuration.\\n\\nUnlike `home.extraDependencies`, these store paths do not\\nbecome part of the built home configuration.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"home\",\"checks\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"list of package\"},\"home.enableDebugInfo\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/misc/debug.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/misc/debug.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"false\"},\"description\":\"Some Nix packages provide debug symbols for\\n{command}`gdb` in the `debug` output.\\nThis option ensures that those are automatically fetched from\\nthe binary cache if available and {command}`gdb` is\\nconfigured to find those symbols.\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"true\"},\"loc\":[\"home\",\"enableDebugInfo\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"home.enableNixpkgsReleaseCheck\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/home-environment.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/home-environment.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"true\"},\"description\":\"Determines whether to check for release version mismatch between Home\\nManager and Nixpkgs. Using mismatched versions is likely to cause errors\\nand unexpected behavior. It is therefore highly recommended to use a\\nrelease of Home Manager that corresponds with your chosen release of\\nNixpkgs.\\n\\nWhen this option is enabled and a mismatch is detected then a warning\\nwill be printed when the user configuration is being built.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"home\",\"enableNixpkgsReleaseCheck\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"home.extraDependencies\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/home-environment.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/home-environment.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"[ ]\"},\"description\":\"A list of paths that should be included in the home\\nclosure but generally not visible.\\n\\nFor built-time checks the `home.checks` option is more appropriate\\nfor that purpose as checks should not leave a trace in the built\\nhome configuration.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"home\",\"extraDependencies\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"list of path in the Nix store\"},\"home.extraOutputsToInstall\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/home-environment.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/home-environment.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"[ ]\"},\"description\":\"List of additional package outputs of the packages\\n{var}`home.packages` that should be installed into\\nthe user environment.\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"[\\n  \\\"doc\\\"\\n  \\\"info\\\"\\n  \\\"devdoc\\\"\\n]\"},\"loc\":[\"home\",\"extraOutputsToInstall\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"list of string\"},\"home.file\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/files.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/files.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"{ }\"},\"description\":\"Attribute set of files to link into the user home.\",\"loc\":[\"home\",\"file\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"attribute set of (submodule)\"},\"home.file.<name>.enable\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/files.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/files.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"true\"},\"description\":\"Whether this file should be generated. This option allows specific\\nfiles to be disabled.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"home\",\"file\",\"<name>\",\"enable\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"home.file.<name>.executable\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/files.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/files.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"Set the execute bit. If `null`, defaults to the mode\\nof the {var}`source` file or to `false`\\nfor files created through the {var}`text` option.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"home\",\"file\",\"<name>\",\"executable\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or boolean\"},\"home.file.<name>.force\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/files.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/files.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"false\"},\"description\":\"Whether the target path should be unconditionally replaced\\nby the managed file source. Warning, this will silently\\ndelete the target regardless of whether it is a file or\\nlink.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"home\",\"file\",\"<name>\",\"force\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"home.file.<name>.ignorelinks\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/files.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/files.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"false\"},\"description\":\"When `recursive` is enabled, adds the `-ignorelinks` flag to lndir.\\n\\nIt causes lndir to not treat symbolic links in the source directory specially.\\nThe link created in the target directory will point back to the corresponding\\nsymbolic link in the source directory. If that link points to a directory, the\\nresulting target will be a link to the source tree's symlink rather than a\\nrecursively linked directory tree.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"home\",\"file\",\"<name>\",\"ignorelinks\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"home.file.<name>.onChange\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/files.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/files.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"\\\"\\\"\"},\"description\":\"Shell commands to run when file has changed between\\ngenerations. The script will be run\\n*after* the new files have been linked\\ninto place.\\n\\nNote, this code is always run when `recursive` is\\nenabled.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"home\",\"file\",\"<name>\",\"onChange\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"strings concatenated with \\\"\\\\n\\\"\"},\"home.file.<name>.recursive\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/files.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/files.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"false\"},\"description\":\"If the file source is a directory, then this option\\ndetermines whether the directory should be recursively\\nlinked to the target location. This option has no effect\\nif the source is a file.\\n\\nIf `false` (the default) then the target\\nwill be a symbolic link to the source directory. If\\n`true` then the target will be a\\ndirectory structure matching the source's but whose leaves\\nare symbolic links to the files of the source directory.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"home\",\"file\",\"<name>\",\"recursive\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"home.file.<name>.source\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/files.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/files.nix\"}],\"description\":\"Path of the source file or directory. If\\n[](#opt-home.file._name_.text)\\nis non-null then this option will automatically point to a file\\ncontaining that text.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"home\",\"file\",\"<name>\",\"source\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"absolute path\"},\"home.file.<name>.target\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/files.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/files.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"name\"},\"description\":\"Path to target file relative to {env}`HOME`.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"home\",\"file\",\"<name>\",\"target\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"non-empty string\"},\"home.file.<name>.text\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/files.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/files.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"Text of the file. If this option is null then\\n[](#opt-home.file._name_.source)\\nmust be set.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"home\",\"file\",\"<name>\",\"text\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or strings concatenated with \\\"\\\\n\\\"\"},\"home.homeDirectory\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/home-environment.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/home-environment.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"\\\"$HOME\\\"   for state version < 20.09,\\nundefined for state version ≥ 20.09\\n\"},\"description\":\"The user's home directory. Must be an absolute path.\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"\\\"/home/jane.doe\\\"\"},\"loc\":[\"home\",\"homeDirectory\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"absolute path\"},\"home.keyboard\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/home-environment.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/home-environment.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"\\\"{ }\\\"  for state version < 21.11,\\n\\\"null\\\" for state version ≥ 21.11\\n\"},\"description\":\"Keyboard configuration. Set to `null` to\\ndisable Home Manager keyboard management.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"home\",\"keyboard\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or (submodule)\"},\"home.keyboard.layout\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/home-environment.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/home-environment.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"Keyboard layout. If `null`, then the system\\nconfiguration will be used.\\n\\nThis defaults to `null` for state\\nversion ≥ 19.09 and `\\\"us\\\"` otherwise.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"home\",\"keyboard\",\"layout\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or string\"},\"home.keyboard.model\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/home-environment.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/home-environment.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"Keyboard model.\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"\\\"presario\\\"\"},\"loc\":[\"home\",\"keyboard\",\"model\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or string\"},\"home.keyboard.options\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/home-environment.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/home-environment.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"[ ]\"},\"description\":\"X keyboard options; layout switching goes here.\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"[\\n  \\\"grp:caps_toggle\\\"\\n  \\\"grp_led:scroll\\\"\\n]\"},\"loc\":[\"home\",\"keyboard\",\"options\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"list of string\"},\"home.keyboard.variant\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/home-environment.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/home-environment.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"X keyboard variant. If `null`, then the\\nsystem configuration will be used.\\n\\nThis defaults to `null` for state\\nversion ≥ 19.09 and `\\\"\\\"` otherwise.\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"\\\"colemak\\\"\"},\"loc\":[\"home\",\"keyboard\",\"variant\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or string\"},\"home.language\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/home-environment.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/home-environment.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"{ }\"},\"description\":\"Language configuration.\",\"loc\":[\"home\",\"language\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"submodule\"},\"home.language.address\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/home-environment.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/home-environment.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"The language to use for addresses.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"home\",\"language\",\"address\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or string\"},\"home.language.base\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/home-environment.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/home-environment.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"The language to use unless overridden by a more specific option.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"home\",\"language\",\"base\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or string\"},\"home.language.collate\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/home-environment.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/home-environment.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"The language to use for collation (alphabetical ordering).\\n\",\"loc\":[\"home\",\"language\",\"collate\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or string\"},\"home.language.ctype\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/home-environment.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/home-environment.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"Character classification category.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"home\",\"language\",\"ctype\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or string\"},\"home.language.measurement\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/home-environment.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/home-environment.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"The language to use for measurement values.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"home\",\"language\",\"measurement\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or string\"},\"home.language.messages\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/home-environment.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/home-environment.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"The language to use for messages, application UI languages, etc.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"home\",\"language\",\"messages\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or string\"},\"home.language.monetary\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/home-environment.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/home-environment.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"The language to use for formatting currencies and money amounts.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"home\",\"language\",\"monetary\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or string\"},\"home.language.name\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/home-environment.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/home-environment.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"The language to use for personal names.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"home\",\"language\",\"name\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or string\"},\"home.language.numeric\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/home-environment.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/home-environment.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"The language to use for numerical values.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"home\",\"language\",\"numeric\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or string\"},\"home.language.paper\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/home-environment.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/home-environment.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"The language to use for paper sizes.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"home\",\"language\",\"paper\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or string\"},\"home.language.telephone\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/home-environment.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/home-environment.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"The language to use for telephone numbers.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"home\",\"language\",\"telephone\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or string\"},\"home.language.time\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/home-environment.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/home-environment.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"The language to use for formatting times.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"home\",\"language\",\"time\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or string\"},\"home.packages\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/home-environment.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/home-environment.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"[ ]\"},\"description\":\"The set of packages to appear in the user environment.\",\"loc\":[\"home\",\"packages\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"list of package\"},\"home.pointerCursor\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/config/home-cursor.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/config/home-cursor.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"Cursor configuration.\\n\\nTop-level options declared under this submodule are backend independent\\noptions. Options declared under namespaces such as `x11`\\nare backend specific options. By default, only backend independent cursor\\nconfigurations are generated. If you need configurations for specific\\nbackends, you can toggle them via the enable option. For example,\\n[](#opt-home.pointerCursor.x11.enable)\\nwill enable x11 cursor configurations.\\n\\nNote that this will merely generate the cursor configurations.\\nTo apply the configurations, the relevant subsystems must also be configured.\\nFor example, [](#opt-home.pointerCursor.gtk.enable) will generate\\nthe gtk cursor configuration, but [](#opt-gtk.enable) needs\\nto be set for it to be applied.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"home\",\"pointerCursor\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or (submodule)\"},\"home.pointerCursor.dotIcons.enable\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/config/home-cursor.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/config/home-cursor.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"true\"},\"description\":\"Whether to enable `.icons` config generation for {option}`home.pointerCursor`\\n.\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"true\"},\"loc\":[\"home\",\"pointerCursor\",\"dotIcons\",\"enable\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"home.pointerCursor.enable\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/config/home-cursor.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/config/home-cursor.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"false\"},\"description\":\"Whether to enable cursor config generation.\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"true\"},\"loc\":[\"home\",\"pointerCursor\",\"enable\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"home.pointerCursor.gtk.enable\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/config/home-cursor.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/config/home-cursor.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"false\"},\"description\":\"Whether to enable gtk config generation for {option}`home.pointerCursor`\\n.\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"true\"},\"loc\":[\"home\",\"pointerCursor\",\"gtk\",\"enable\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"home.pointerCursor.gtk.size\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/config/home-cursor.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/config/home-cursor.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"\\\"config.home.pointerCursor.size\\\"\"},\"description\":\"The cursor size for gtk.\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"32\"},\"loc\":[\"home\",\"pointerCursor\",\"gtk\",\"size\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"signed integer\"},\"home.pointerCursor.hyprcursor.enable\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/config/home-cursor.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/config/home-cursor.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"false\"},\"description\":\"Whether to enable hyprcursor config generation.\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"true\"},\"loc\":[\"home\",\"pointerCursor\",\"hyprcursor\",\"enable\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"home.pointerCursor.hyprcursor.size\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/config/home-cursor.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/config/home-cursor.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"\\\"config.home.pointerCursor.size\\\"\"},\"description\":\"The cursor size for hyprcursor.\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"32\"},\"loc\":[\"home\",\"pointerCursor\",\"hyprcursor\",\"size\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"signed integer\"},\"home.pointerCursor.name\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/config/home-cursor.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/config/home-cursor.nix\"}],\"description\":\"The cursor name within the package.\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"\\\"Vanilla-DMZ\\\"\"},\"loc\":[\"home\",\"pointerCursor\",\"name\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"string\"},\"home.pointerCursor.package\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/config/home-cursor.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/config/home-cursor.nix\"}],\"description\":\"Package providing the cursor theme.\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"pkgs.vanilla-dmz\"},\"loc\":[\"home\",\"pointerCursor\",\"package\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"package\"},\"home.pointerCursor.size\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/config/home-cursor.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/config/home-cursor.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"32\"},\"description\":\"The cursor size.\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"64\"},\"loc\":[\"home\",\"pointerCursor\",\"size\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"signed integer\"},\"home.pointerCursor.sway.enable\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/config/home-cursor.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/config/home-cursor.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"false\"},\"description\":\"Whether to enable sway config generation for {option}`home.pointerCursor`.\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"true\"},\"loc\":[\"home\",\"pointerCursor\",\"sway\",\"enable\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"home.pointerCursor.sway.size\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/config/home-cursor.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/config/home-cursor.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"\\\"config.home.pointerCursor.size\\\"\"},\"description\":\"The cursor size for sway.\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"32\"},\"loc\":[\"home\",\"pointerCursor\",\"sway\",\"size\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"signed integer\"},\"home.pointerCursor.x11.defaultCursor\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/config/home-cursor.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/config/home-cursor.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"\\\"left_ptr\\\"\"},\"description\":\"The default cursor file to use within the package.\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"\\\"X_cursor\\\"\"},\"loc\":[\"home\",\"pointerCursor\",\"x11\",\"defaultCursor\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"string\"},\"home.pointerCursor.x11.enable\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/config/home-cursor.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/config/home-cursor.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"false\"},\"description\":\"Whether to enable x11 config generation for {option}`home.pointerCursor`\\n.\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"true\"},\"loc\":[\"home\",\"pointerCursor\",\"x11\",\"enable\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"home.pointerCursor.x11.size\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/config/home-cursor.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/config/home-cursor.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"\\\"config.home.pointerCursor.size\\\"\"},\"description\":\"The cursor size for x11.\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"32\"},\"loc\":[\"home\",\"pointerCursor\",\"x11\",\"size\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"signed integer\"},\"home.preferXdgDirectories\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/home-environment.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/home-environment.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"false\"},\"description\":\"Whether to make programs use XDG directories whenever supported.\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"true\"},\"loc\":[\"home\",\"preferXdgDirectories\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"home.profileDirectory\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/home-environment.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/home-environment.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"\\\"${home.homeDirectory}/.nix-profile\\\"  or\\n\\\"/etc/profiles/per-user/${home.username}\\\"\\n\"},\"description\":\"The profile directory where Home Manager generations are installed.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"home\",\"profileDirectory\"],\"readOnly\":true,\"type\":\"absolute path\"},\"home.services\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/services-modular>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/services-modular\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"{ }\"},\"description\":\"Home Manager [modular services](https://nixos.org/manual/nixos/unstable/#modular-services).\\n\\nEach entry is an abstract service that may declare a {option}`process.argv`\\nand Home Manager-style {option}`systemd.user.{services,sockets}` units\\n(INI section shape). Units are emitted under Home Manager's\\n{option}`systemd.user.services` (and friends) with the service name\\nas a prefix. Mirrors {option}`system.services` in NixOS.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"home\",\"services\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"attribute set of (submodule)\"},\"home.sessionPath\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/home-environment.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/home-environment.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"[ ]\"},\"description\":\"Extra directories to prepend to {env}`PATH`.\\n\\nThese directories are added to the {env}`PATH` variable in a\\ndouble-quoted context, so expressions like `$HOME` are\\nexpanded by the shell. However, since expressions like `~` or\\n`*` are escaped, they will end up in the {env}`PATH`\\nverbatim.\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"[\\n  \\\"$HOME/.local/bin\\\"\\n  \\\"\\\\${xdg.configHome}/emacs/bin\\\"\\n  \\\".git/safe/../../bin\\\"\\n]\"},\"loc\":[\"home\",\"sessionPath\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"list of string\"},\"home.sessionSearchVariables\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/home-environment.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/home-environment.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"{ }\"},\"description\":\"Extra directories to prepend to arbitrary PATH-like\\nenvironment variables (e.g.: {env}`MANPATH`). The values\\nwill be concatenated by `:`.\\nThese directories are added to the environment variable in a\\ndouble-quoted context, so expressions like `$HOME` are\\nexpanded by the shell. However, since expressions like `~` or\\n`*` are escaped, they will end up in the environment\\nverbatim.\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"{\\n  MANPATH = [\\n    \\\"$HOME/.npm-packages/man\\\"\\n    \\\"\\\\${xdg.configHome}/.local/share/man\\\"\\n  ];\\n}\"},\"loc\":[\"home\",\"sessionSearchVariables\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"attribute set of list of string\"},\"home.sessionVariables\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/home-environment.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/home-environment.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"{ }\"},\"description\":\"Environment variables to always set at login.\\n\\nThe values may refer to other environment variables using\\nPOSIX.2 style variable references. For example, a variable\\n{var}`parameter` may be referenced as\\n`$parameter` or `${parameter}`. A\\ndefault value `foo` may be given as per\\n`${parameter:-foo}` and, similarly, an alternate\\nvalue `bar` can be given as per\\n`${parameter:+bar}`.\\n\\nNote, these variables may be set in any order so no session\\nvariable may have a runtime dependency on another session\\nvariable. In particular code like\\n```nix\\nhome.sessionVariables = {\\n  FOO = \\\"Hello\\\";\\n  BAR = \\\"$FOO World!\\\";\\n};\\n```\\nmay not work as expected. If you need to reference another\\nsession variable (even if it is declared by using other options\\nlike [](#opt-xdg.configHome)), then do so inside Nix instead.\\nThe above example then becomes\\n```nix\\nhome.sessionVariables = {\\n  FOO = \\\"Hello\\\";\\n  BAR = \\\"${config.home.sessionVariables.FOO} World!\\\";\\n};\\n```\\n\\nSetting a value to `null` will skip setting the variable at all, which\\nmay be useful when overriding.\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"{\\n  EDITOR = \\\"emacs\\\";\\n  GS_OPTIONS = \\\"-sPAPERSIZE=a4\\\";\\n}\"},\"loc\":[\"home\",\"sessionVariables\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"lazy attribute set of (null or string or absolute path or signed integer or floating point number or boolean)\"},\"home.shell.enableBashIntegration\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/misc/shell.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/misc/shell.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalMD\",\"text\":\"[](#opt-home.shell.enableShellIntegration)\"},\"description\":\"Whether to enable Bash integration.\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"false\"},\"loc\":[\"home\",\"shell\",\"enableBashIntegration\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"home.shell.enableFishIntegration\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/misc/shell.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/misc/shell.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalMD\",\"text\":\"[](#opt-home.shell.enableShellIntegration)\"},\"description\":\"Whether to enable Fish integration.\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"false\"},\"loc\":[\"home\",\"shell\",\"enableFishIntegration\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"home.shell.enableIonIntegration\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/misc/shell.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/misc/shell.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalMD\",\"text\":\"[](#opt-home.shell.enableShellIntegration)\"},\"description\":\"Whether to enable Ion integration.\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"false\"},\"loc\":[\"home\",\"shell\",\"enableIonIntegration\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"home.shell.enableNushellIntegration\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/misc/shell.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/misc/shell.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalMD\",\"text\":\"[](#opt-home.shell.enableShellIntegration)\"},\"description\":\"Whether to enable Nushell integration.\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"false\"},\"loc\":[\"home\",\"shell\",\"enableNushellIntegration\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"home.shell.enableShellIntegration\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/misc/shell.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/misc/shell.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"true\"},\"description\":\"Whether to globally enable shell integration for all supported shells.\\n\\nIndividual shell integrations can be overridden with their respective\\n`shell.enable<SHELL>Integration` option. For example, the following\\ndeclaration globally disables shell integration for Bash:\\n\\n```nix\\nhome.shell.enableBashIntegration = false;\\n```\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"false\"},\"loc\":[\"home\",\"shell\",\"enableShellIntegration\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"home.shell.enableZshIntegration\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/misc/shell.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/misc/shell.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalMD\",\"text\":\"[](#opt-home.shell.enableShellIntegration)\"},\"description\":\"Whether to enable Zsh integration.\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"false\"},\"loc\":[\"home\",\"shell\",\"enableZshIntegration\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"home.shellAliases\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/home-environment.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/home-environment.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"{ }\"},\"description\":\"An attribute set that maps aliases (the top level attribute names\\nin this option) to command strings or directly to build outputs.\\n\\nThis option should only be used to manage simple aliases that are\\ncompatible across all shells. If you need to use a shell specific\\nfeature then make sure to use a shell specific option, for example\\n[](#opt-programs.bash.shellAliases) for Bash.\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"{\\n  g = \\\"git\\\";\\n  \\\"...\\\" = \\\"cd ../..\\\";\\n}\\n\"},\"loc\":[\"home\",\"shellAliases\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"attribute set of string\"},\"home.stateVersion\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/misc/version.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/misc/version.nix\"}],\"description\":\"It is occasionally necessary for Home Manager to change\\nconfiguration defaults in a way that is incompatible with\\nstateful data. This could, for example, include switching the\\ndefault data format or location of a file.\\n\\nThe *state version* indicates which default\\nsettings are in effect and will therefore help avoid breaking\\nprogram configurations. Switching to a higher state version\\ntypically requires performing some manual steps, such as data\\nconversion or moving files.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"home\",\"stateVersion\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"one of \\\"18.09\\\", \\\"19.03\\\", \\\"19.09\\\", \\\"20.03\\\", \\\"20.09\\\", \\\"21.03\\\", \\\"21.05\\\", \\\"21.11\\\", \\\"22.05\\\", \\\"22.11\\\", \\\"23.05\\\", \\\"23.11\\\", \\\"24.05\\\", \\\"24.11\\\", \\\"25.05\\\", \\\"25.11\\\", \\\"26.05\\\"\"},\"home.uid\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/home-environment.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/home-environment.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"The user's uid.\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"1000\"},\"loc\":[\"home\",\"uid\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or (unsigned integer, meaning >=0)\"},\"home.username\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/home-environment.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/home-environment.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"\\\"$USER\\\"   for state version < 20.09,\\nundefined for state version ≥ 20.09\\n\"},\"description\":\"The user's username.\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"\\\"jane.doe\\\"\"},\"loc\":[\"home\",\"username\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"string\"},\"i18n.glibcLocales\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/config/i18n.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/config/i18n.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"nixosConfig.i18n.glibcLocales or pkgs.glibcLocales\"},\"description\":\"Customized `glibcLocales` package providing\\nthe `LOCALE_ARCHIVE_*` environment variable.\\n\\nThis option only applies to the Linux platform.\\n\\nIf Home Manager is installed as a NixOS submodule, this\\noption defaults to NixOS' {var}`i18n.glibcLocales`.\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"pkgs.glibcLocales.override {\\n  allLocales = false;\\n  locales = [ \\\"en_US.UTF-8/UTF-8\\\" ];\\n}\\n\"},\"loc\":[\"i18n\",\"glibcLocales\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"absolute path\"},\"i18n.inputMethod.enable\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/i18n/input-method/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/i18n/input-method/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalMD\",\"text\":\"`true` if the deprecated option `enabled` is set, false otherwise\"},\"description\":\"Whether to enable an additional input method type.\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"true\"},\"loc\":[\"i18n\",\"inputMethod\",\"enable\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"i18n.inputMethod.enabled\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/i18n/input-method/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/i18n/input-method/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"Deprecated - use `type` and `enable = true` instead\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"\\\"fcitx5\\\"\"},\"loc\":[\"i18n\",\"inputMethod\",\"enabled\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or one of \\\"fcitx\\\", \\\"fcitx5\\\", \\\"nabi\\\", \\\"uim\\\", \\\"hime\\\", \\\"kime\\\"\"},\"i18n.inputMethod.fcitx5.addons\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/i18n/input-method/fcitx5.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/i18n/input-method/fcitx5.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"[ ]\"},\"description\":\"Enabled Fcitx5 addons.\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"with pkgs; [ fcitx5-rime ]\"},\"loc\":[\"i18n\",\"inputMethod\",\"fcitx5\",\"addons\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"list of package\"},\"i18n.inputMethod.fcitx5.fcitx5-with-addons\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/i18n/input-method/fcitx5.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/i18n/input-method/fcitx5.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"<derivation fcitx5-with-addons-5.1.19>\"},\"description\":\"The fcitx5 package to use.\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"pkgs.kdePackages.fcitx5-with-addons\"},\"loc\":[\"i18n\",\"inputMethod\",\"fcitx5\",\"fcitx5-with-addons\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"package\"},\"i18n.inputMethod.fcitx5.ignoreUserConfig\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/i18n/input-method/fcitx5.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/i18n/input-method/fcitx5.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"false\"},\"description\":\"Ignore the user configures. **Warning**: When this is enabled, the\\nuser config files are totally ignored and the user dict can't be saved\\nand loaded.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"i18n\",\"inputMethod\",\"fcitx5\",\"ignoreUserConfig\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"i18n.inputMethod.fcitx5.quickPhrase\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/i18n/input-method/fcitx5.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/i18n/input-method/fcitx5.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"{ }\"},\"description\":\"Quick phrases.\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"{\\n  angry = \\\"(￣ー￣)\\\";\\n  smile = \\\"（・∀・）\\\";\\n}\"},\"loc\":[\"i18n\",\"inputMethod\",\"fcitx5\",\"quickPhrase\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"attribute set of string\"},\"i18n.inputMethod.fcitx5.quickPhraseFiles\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/i18n/input-method/fcitx5.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/i18n/input-method/fcitx5.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"{ }\"},\"description\":\"Quick phrase files.\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"{\\n  words = ./words.mb;\\n  numbers = ./numbers.mb;\\n}\\n\"},\"loc\":[\"i18n\",\"inputMethod\",\"fcitx5\",\"quickPhraseFiles\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"attribute set of absolute path\"},\"i18n.inputMethod.fcitx5.settings.addons\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/i18n/input-method/fcitx5.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/i18n/input-method/fcitx5.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"{ }\"},\"description\":\"The addon configures in `conf` folder in ini format with global sections.\\nEach item is written to the corresponding file.\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"{\\n  classicui = {\\n    globalSection = {\\n      Theme = \\\"example\\\";\\n    };\\n  };\\n  pinyin = {\\n    globalSection = {\\n      EmojiEnabled = \\\"True\\\";\\n    };\\n  };\\n}\"},\"loc\":[\"i18n\",\"inputMethod\",\"fcitx5\",\"settings\",\"addons\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"attribute set of (submodule)\"},\"i18n.inputMethod.fcitx5.settings.addons.<name>.globalSection\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/i18n/input-method/fcitx5.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/i18n/input-method/fcitx5.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"{ }\"},\"description\":\"global section of an INI file (attrs of INI atom (null, bool, int, float or string))\",\"loc\":[\"i18n\",\"inputMethod\",\"fcitx5\",\"settings\",\"addons\",\"<name>\",\"globalSection\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"section of an INI file (attrs of INI atom (null, bool, int, float or string))\"},\"i18n.inputMethod.fcitx5.settings.addons.<name>.sections\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/i18n/input-method/fcitx5.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/i18n/input-method/fcitx5.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"{ }\"},\"description\":\"attribute set of section of an INI file (attrs of INI atom (null, bool, int, float or string))\",\"loc\":[\"i18n\",\"inputMethod\",\"fcitx5\",\"settings\",\"addons\",\"<name>\",\"sections\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"attribute set of section of an INI file (attrs of INI atom (null, bool, int, float or string))\"},\"i18n.inputMethod.fcitx5.settings.globalOptions\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/i18n/input-method/fcitx5.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/i18n/input-method/fcitx5.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"{ }\"},\"description\":\"The global options in `config` file in ini format.\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"{\\n  Behavior = {\\n    ActiveByDefault = false;\\n  };\\n  Hotkey = {\\n    EnumerateSkipFirst = false;\\n    EnumerateWithTriggerKeys = true;\\n    ModifierOnlyKeyTimeout = 250;\\n  };\\n}\"},\"loc\":[\"i18n\",\"inputMethod\",\"fcitx5\",\"settings\",\"globalOptions\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"open submodule of attribute set of section of an INI file (attrs of INI atom (null, bool, int, float or string))\"},\"i18n.inputMethod.fcitx5.settings.inputMethod\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/i18n/input-method/fcitx5.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/i18n/input-method/fcitx5.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"{ }\"},\"description\":\"The input method configure in `profile` file in ini format.\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"{\\n  GroupOrder = {\\n    \\\"0\\\" = \\\"Default\\\";\\n  };\\n  \\\"Groups/0\\\" = {\\n    \\\"Default Layout\\\" = \\\"us\\\";\\n    DefaultIM = \\\"pinyin\\\";\\n    Name = \\\"Default\\\";\\n  };\\n  \\\"Groups/0/Items/0\\\" = {\\n    Name = \\\"keyboard-us\\\";\\n  };\\n  \\\"Groups/0/Items/1\\\" = {\\n    Name = \\\"pinyin\\\";\\n  };\\n}\"},\"loc\":[\"i18n\",\"inputMethod\",\"fcitx5\",\"settings\",\"inputMethod\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"open submodule of attribute set of section of an INI file (attrs of INI atom (null, bool, int, float or string))\"},\"i18n.inputMethod.fcitx5.themes\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/i18n/input-method/fcitx5.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/i18n/input-method/fcitx5.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"{ }\"},\"description\":\"Themes to be written to {file}`$XDG_DATA_HOME/fcitx5/themes/${name}`\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"\\\"\\\"\"},\"loc\":[\"i18n\",\"inputMethod\",\"fcitx5\",\"themes\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"lazy attribute set of (submodule)\"},\"i18n.inputMethod.fcitx5.themes.<name>.highlightImage\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/i18n/input-method/fcitx5.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/i18n/input-method/fcitx5.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"Path to the SVG of the highlight.\",\"loc\":[\"i18n\",\"inputMethod\",\"fcitx5\",\"themes\",\"<name>\",\"highlightImage\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or absolute path\"},\"i18n.inputMethod.fcitx5.themes.<name>.panelImage\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/i18n/input-method/fcitx5.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/i18n/input-method/fcitx5.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"Path to the SVG of the panel.\",\"loc\":[\"i18n\",\"inputMethod\",\"fcitx5\",\"themes\",\"<name>\",\"panelImage\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or absolute path\"},\"i18n.inputMethod.fcitx5.themes.<name>.theme\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/i18n/input-method/fcitx5.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/i18n/input-method/fcitx5.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"The `theme.conf` file of the theme.\\n\\nSee https://fcitx-im.org/wiki/Fcitx_5_Theme#Background_images\\nfor more information.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"i18n\",\"inputMethod\",\"fcitx5\",\"themes\",\"<name>\",\"theme\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or (attribute set of section of an INI file (attrs of INI atom (null, bool, int, float or string))) or strings concatenated with \\\"\\\\n\\\" or absolute path\"},\"i18n.inputMethod.fcitx5.waylandFrontend\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/i18n/input-method/fcitx5.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/i18n/input-method/fcitx5.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"false\"},\"description\":\"Use the Wayland input method frontend.\\nSee [Using Fcitx 5 on Wayland](https://fcitx-im.org/wiki/Using_Fcitx_5_on_Wayland).\\n\",\"loc\":[\"i18n\",\"inputMethod\",\"fcitx5\",\"waylandFrontend\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"i18n.inputMethod.kime.extraConfig\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/i18n/input-method/kime.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/i18n/input-method/kime.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"\\\"\\\"\"},\"description\":\"kime configuration. Refer to\\n<https://github.com/Riey/kime/blob/develop/docs/CONFIGURATION.md>\\nfor details on supported values.\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"daemon:\\n  modules: [Xim,Indicator]\\nindicator:\\n  icon_color: White\\nengine:\\n  hangul:\\n    layout: dubeolsik\\n\"},\"loc\":[\"i18n\",\"inputMethod\",\"kime\",\"extraConfig\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"strings concatenated with \\\"\\\\n\\\"\"},\"i18n.inputMethod.type\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/i18n/input-method/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/i18n/input-method/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalMD\",\"text\":\"The value of the deprecated option `enabled`, defaulting to null\"},\"description\":\"Select the enabled input method. Input methods are software to input\\nsymbols that are not available on standard input devices.\\n\\nInput methods are especially used to input Chinese, Japanese and\\nKorean characters.\\n\\nCurrently the following input methods are available in Home Manager:\\n\\n`fcitx5`\\n: A customizable lightweight input method.\\n  The next generation of fcitx.\\n  Addons (including engines, dictionaries, skins) can be added using\\n  [](#opt-i18n.inputMethod.fcitx5.addons).\\n\\n`nabi`\\n: A Korean input method based on XIM. Nabi doesn't support Qt 5.\\n\\n`uim`\\n: The \\\"universal input method\\\" is a library with an XIM bridge.\\n  uim mainly supports Chinese, Japanese and Korean.\\n\\n`hime`\\n: An extremely easy-to-use input method framework.\\n\\n`kime`\\n: A Korean IME.\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"\\\"fcitx5\\\"\"},\"loc\":[\"i18n\",\"inputMethod\",\"type\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or one of \\\"fcitx\\\", \\\"fcitx5\\\", \\\"nabi\\\", \\\"uim\\\", \\\"hime\\\", \\\"kime\\\"\"},\"i18n.inputMethod.uim.toolbar\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/i18n/input-method/uim.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/i18n/input-method/uim.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"\\\"gtk\\\"\"},\"description\":\"Selected UIM toolbar.\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"\\\"gtk-systray\\\"\"},\"loc\":[\"i18n\",\"inputMethod\",\"uim\",\"toolbar\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"one of \\\"gtk\\\", \\\"gtk3\\\", \\\"gtk-systray\\\", \\\"gtk3-systray\\\", \\\"qt4\\\"\"},\"launchd.agents\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"{ }\"},\"description\":\"Define LaunchAgents.\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"attribute set of (submodule)\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"{ }\"},\"description\":\"Define a launchd job. See {manpage}`launchd.plist(5)` for details.\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"{\\n  ProgramArguments = [\\n    \\\"/usr/bin/say\\\"\\n    \\\"Good afternoon\\\"\\n  ];\\n  StartCalendarInterval = [\\n    {\\n      Hour = 12;\\n      Minute = 0;\\n    }\\n  ];\\n}\"},\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"open submodule of attribute set of anything\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.AbandonProcessGroup\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"When a job dies, launchd kills any remaining processes with the same process group ID as the job. Setting\\nthis key to true disables that behavior.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"AbandonProcessGroup\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or boolean\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.Debug\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"This optional key specifies that launchd should adjust its log mask temporarily to LOG_DEBUG while\\ndealing with this job.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"Debug\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or boolean\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.Disabled\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"This optional key is used as a hint to `launchctl(1)` that it should not submit this job to launchd when\\nloading a job or jobs. The value of this key does NOT reflect the current state of the job on the running\\nsystem. If you wish to know whether a job is loaded in launchd, reading this key from a configuration\\nfile yourself is not a sufficient test. You should query launchd for the presence of the job using\\nthe `launchctl(1)` list subcommand or use the ServiceManagement framework's\\n`SMJobCopyDictionary()` method.\\n\\nNote that as of Mac OS X v10.6, this key's value in a configuration file conveys a default value, which\\nis changed with the [-w] option of the `launchctl(1)` load and unload subcommands. These subcommands no\\nlonger modify the configuration file, so the value displayed in the configuration file is not necessarily\\nthe value that `launchctl(1)` will apply. See `launchctl(1)` for more information.\\n\\nPlease also be mindful that you should only use this key if the provided on-demand and KeepAlive criteria\\nare insufficient to describe the conditions under which your job needs to run. The cost to have a\\njob loaded in launchd is negligible, so there is no harm in loading a job which only runs once or very\\nrarely.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"Disabled\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or boolean\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.EnableGlobbing\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"This flag causes launchd to use the `glob(3)` mechanism to update the program arguments before invocation.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"EnableGlobbing\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or boolean\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.EnableTransactions\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"This flag instructs launchd that the job promises to use `vproc_transaction_begin(3)` and\\n`vproc_transaction_end(3)` to track outstanding transactions that need to be reconciled before the\\nprocess can safely terminate. If no outstanding transactions are in progress, then launchd is free to\\nsend the SIGKILL signal.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"EnableTransactions\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or boolean\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.EnvironmentVariables\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"This optional key is used to specify additional environment variables to be set before running the\\njob.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"EnvironmentVariables\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or (attribute set of string)\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.ExitTimeOut\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"The amount of time launchd waits before sending a SIGKILL signal. The default value is 20 seconds. The\\nvalue zero is interpreted as infinity.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"ExitTimeOut\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or signed integer\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.GroupName\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"This optional key specifies the group to run the job as. This key is only applicable when launchd is\\nrunning as root. If UserName is set and GroupName is not, the the group will be set to the default\\ngroup of the user.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"GroupName\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or string\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.HardResourceLimits\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"Resource limits to be imposed on the job. These adjust variables set with `setrlimit(2)`.  The following\\nkeys apply:\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"{\\n  NumberOfFiles = 4096;\\n}\"},\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"HardResourceLimits\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or (submodule)\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.HardResourceLimits.CPU\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"The maximum amount of cpu time (in seconds) to be used by each process.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"HardResourceLimits\",\"CPU\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or signed integer\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.HardResourceLimits.Core\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"The largest size (in bytes) core file that may be created.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"HardResourceLimits\",\"Core\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or signed integer\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.HardResourceLimits.Data\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"The maximum size (in bytes) of the data segment for a process; this defines how far a program may\\nextend its break with the `sbrk(2)` system call.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"HardResourceLimits\",\"Data\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or signed integer\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.HardResourceLimits.FileSize\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"The largest size (in bytes) file that may be created.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"HardResourceLimits\",\"FileSize\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or signed integer\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.HardResourceLimits.MemoryLock\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"The maximum size (in bytes) which a process may lock into memory using the `mlock(2)` function.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"HardResourceLimits\",\"MemoryLock\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or signed integer\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.HardResourceLimits.NumberOfFiles\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"The maximum number of open files for this process.  Setting this value in a system wide daemon\\nwill set the `sysctl(3)` kern.maxfiles (SoftResourceLimits) or kern.maxfilesperproc (HardResourceLimits)\\nvalue in addition to the `setrlimit(2)` values.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"HardResourceLimits\",\"NumberOfFiles\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or signed integer\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.HardResourceLimits.NumberOfProcesses\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"The maximum number of simultaneous processes for this user id.  Setting this value in a system\\nwide daemon will set the `sysctl(3)` kern.maxproc (SoftResourceLimits) or kern.maxprocperuid\\n(HardResourceLimits) value in addition to the `setrlimit(2)` values.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"HardResourceLimits\",\"NumberOfProcesses\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or signed integer\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.HardResourceLimits.ResidentSetSize\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"The maximum size (in bytes) to which a process's resident set size may grow.  This imposes a\\nlimit on the amount of physical memory to be given to a process; if memory is tight, the system\\nwill prefer to take memory from processes that are exceeding their declared resident set size.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"HardResourceLimits\",\"ResidentSetSize\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or signed integer\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.HardResourceLimits.Stack\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"The maximum size (in bytes) of the stack segment for a process; this defines how far a program's\\nstack segment may be extended.  Stack extension is performed automatically by the system.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"HardResourceLimits\",\"Stack\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or signed integer\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.InitGroups\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"This optional key specifies whether `initgroups(3)` should be called before running the job.  The default\\nis true in 10.5 and false in 10.4. This key will be ignored if the UserName key is not set.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"InitGroups\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or boolean\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.KeepAlive\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"This optional key is used to control whether your job is to be kept continuously running or to let\\ndemand and conditions control the invocation. The default is false and therefore only demand will start\\nthe job. The value may be set to true to unconditionally keep the job alive. Alternatively, a dictionary\\nof conditions may be specified to selectively control whether launchd keeps a job alive or not. If\\nmultiple keys are provided, launchd ORs them, thus providing maximum flexibility to the job to refine\\nthe logic and stall if necessary. If launchd finds no reason to restart the job, it falls back on\\ndemand based invocation.  Jobs that exit quickly and frequently when configured to be kept alive will\\nbe throttled to conserve system resources.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"KeepAlive\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or boolean or (submodule)\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.KeepAlive.AfterInitialDemand\":{\"declarations\":[],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"Whether to defer evaluating other `KeepAlive` conditions until\\nthe job has been started at least once by demand.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"KeepAlive\",\"AfterInitialDemand\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or boolean\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.KeepAlive.Crashed\":{\"declarations\":[],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"If true, the the job will be restarted as long as it exited due to a signal which is typically\\nassociated with a crash (SIGILL, SIGSEGV, etc.). If false, the job will be restarted in the\\ninverse condition.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"KeepAlive\",\"Crashed\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or boolean\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.KeepAlive.NetworkState\":{\"declarations\":[],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"If true, the job will be kept alive as long as the network is up, where up is defined as at least\\none non-loopback interface being up and having IPv4 or IPv6 addresses assigned to them.  If\\nfalse, the job will be kept alive in the inverse condition.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"KeepAlive\",\"NetworkState\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or boolean\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.KeepAlive.OtherJobEnabled\":{\"declarations\":[],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"Each key in this dictionary is the label of another job. If the value of the key is true, then\\nthis job is kept alive as long as that other job is enabled. Otherwise, if the value is false,\\nthen this job is kept alive as long as the other job is disabled.  This feature should not be\\nconsidered a substitute for the use of IPC.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"KeepAlive\",\"OtherJobEnabled\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or (attribute set of boolean)\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.KeepAlive.PathState\":{\"declarations\":[],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"Each key in this dictionary is a file-system path. If the value of the key is true, then the job\\nwill be kept alive as long as the path exists.  If false, the job will be kept alive in the\\ninverse condition. The intent of this feature is that two or more jobs may create semaphores in\\nthe file-system namespace.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"KeepAlive\",\"PathState\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or (attribute set of boolean)\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.KeepAlive.SuccessfulExit\":{\"declarations\":[],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"If true, the job will be restarted as long as the program exits and with an exit status of zero.\\nIf false, the job will be restarted in the inverse condition.  This key implies that \\\"RunAtLoad\\\"\\nis set to true, since the job needs to run at least once before we can get an exit status.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"KeepAlive\",\"SuccessfulExit\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or boolean\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.Label\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"description\":\"This required key uniquely identifies the job to launchd.\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"Label\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"string\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.LaunchEvents\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"Specifies higher-level event types to be used as launch-on-demand event\\nsources.  Each sub-dictionary defines events for a particular event\\nsubsystem, such as \\\"com.apple.iokit.matching\\\", which can be used to\\nlaunch jobs based on the appearance of nodes in the IORegistry. Each\\ndictionary within the sub-dictionary specifies an event descriptor that\\nis specified to each event subsystem. With this key, the job promises to\\nuse the xpc_set_event_stream_handler(3) API to consume events. See\\nxpc_events(3) for more details on event sources.\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"{\\n  \\\"com.apple.iokit.matching\\\" = {\\n    \\\"com.apple.usb.device\\\" = {\\n      IOMatchLaunchStream = true;\\n      IOProviderClass = \\\"IOUSBDevice\\\";\\n      idProduct = \\\"*\\\";\\n      idVendor = \\\"*\\\";\\n    };\\n  };\\n}\"},\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"LaunchEvents\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or (attribute set)\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.LaunchOnlyOnce\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"This optional key specifies whether the job can only be run once and only once.  In other words, if the\\njob cannot be safely respawned without a full machine reboot, then set this key to be true.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"LaunchOnlyOnce\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or boolean\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.LimitLoadFromHosts\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"This configuration file only applies to hosts NOT listed with this key. Note: One should set kern.hostname\\nin `sysctl.conf(5)` for this feature to work reliably.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"LimitLoadFromHosts\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or (list of string)\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.LimitLoadToHosts\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"This configuration file only applies to the hosts listed with this key. Note: One should set kern.hostname\\nin `sysctl.conf(5)` for this feature to work reliably.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"LimitLoadToHosts\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or (list of string)\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.LimitLoadToSessionType\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"This configuration file only applies to sessions of the type specified. This key is used in concert\\nwith the -S flag to {command}`launchctl`.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"LimitLoadToSessionType\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or string or list of string\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.LowPriorityBackgroundIO\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"This optional key specifies whether the kernel should consider this daemon to be low priority when\\ndoing file system I/O when the process is throttled with the Darwin-background classification.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"LowPriorityBackgroundIO\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or boolean\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.LowPriorityIO\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"This optional key specifies whether the kernel should consider this daemon to be low priority when\\ndoing file system I/O.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"LowPriorityIO\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or boolean\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.MachServices\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"This optional key is used to specify Mach services to be registered with the Mach bootstrap sub-system.\\nEach key in this dictionary should be the name of service to be advertised. The value of the key must\\nbe a boolean and set to true.  Alternatively, a dictionary can be used instead of a simple true value.\\n\\nFinally, for the job itself, the values will be replaced with Mach ports at the time of check-in with\\nlaunchd.\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"{\\n  \\\"org.nixos.service\\\" = {\\n    ResetAtClose = true;\\n  };\\n}\"},\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"MachServices\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or (attribute set of (boolean or (submodule)))\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.MachServices.<name>.HideUntilCheckIn\":{\"declarations\":[],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"Reserve the name in the namespace, but cause bootstrap_look_up() to fail until the job has\\nchecked in with launchd.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"MachServices\",\"<name>\",\"HideUntilCheckIn\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or boolean\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.MachServices.<name>.ResetAtClose\":{\"declarations\":[],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"If this boolean is false, the port is recycled, thus leaving clients to remain oblivious to the\\ndemand nature of job. If the value is set to true, clients receive port death notifications when\\nthe job lets go of the receive right. The port will be recreated atomically with respect to bootstrap_look_up()\\ncalls, so that clients can trust that after receiving a port death notification,\\nthe new port will have already been recreated. Setting the value to true should be done with\\ncare. Not all clients may be able to handle this behavior. The default value is false.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"MachServices\",\"<name>\",\"ResetAtClose\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or boolean\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.Nice\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"This optional key specifies what nice(3) value should be applied to the daemon.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"Nice\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or signed integer\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.OnDemand\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"This key was used in Mac OS X 10.4 to control whether a job was kept alive or not. The default was\\ntrue.  This key has been deprecated and replaced in Mac OS X 10.5 and later with the more powerful\\nKeepAlive option.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"OnDemand\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or boolean\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.ProcessType\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"This optional key describes, at a high level, the intended purpose of the job.  The system will apply\\nresource limits based on what kind of job it is. If left unspecified, the system will apply light\\nresource limits to the job, throttling its CPU usage and I/O bandwidth. The following are valid values:\\n\\nBackground\\n: Background jobs are generally processes that do work that was not directly requested by the user.\\n  The resource limits applied to Background jobs are intended to prevent them from disrupting the\\n  user experience.\\n\\nStandard\\n: Standard jobs are equivalent to no ProcessType being set.\\n\\nAdaptive\\n: Adaptive jobs move between the Background and Interactive classifications based on activity over\\n  XPC connections. See `xpc_transaction_begin(3)` for details.\\n\\nInteractive\\n: Interactive jobs run with the same resource limitations as apps, that is to say, none. Interactive\\n  jobs are critical to maintaining a responsive user experience, and this key should only be\\n  used if an app's ability to be responsive depends on it, and cannot be made Adaptive.\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"\\\"Background\\\"\"},\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"ProcessType\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or one of \\\"Background\\\", \\\"Standard\\\", \\\"Adaptive\\\", \\\"Interactive\\\"\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.Program\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"This key maps to the first argument of `execvp(3)`.  If this key is missing, then the first element of\\nthe array of strings provided to the ProgramArguments will be used instead.  This key is required in\\nthe absence of the ProgramArguments key.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"Program\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or absolute path\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.ProgramArguments\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"This key maps to the second argument of `execvp(3)`.  This key is required in the absence of the Program\\nkey. Please note: many people are confused by this key. Please read `execvp(3)` very carefully!\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"ProgramArguments\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or (list of string)\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.QueueDirectories\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"Much like the WatchPaths option, this key will watch the paths for modifications. The difference being\\nthat the job will only be started if the path is a directory and the directory is not empty.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"QueueDirectories\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or (list of string)\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.RootDirectory\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"This optional key is used to specify a directory to `chroot(2)` to before running the job.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"RootDirectory\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or string\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.RunAtLoad\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"This optional key is used to control whether your job is launched once at the time the job is loaded.\\nThe default is false.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"RunAtLoad\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or boolean\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.ServiceIPC\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"This optional key specifies whether the job participates in advanced\\ncommunication with launchd. The default is false. This flag is\\nincompatible with the inetdCompatibility key.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"ServiceIPC\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or boolean\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.SessionCreate\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"This key specifies that the job should be spawned into a new security\\naudit session rather than the default session for the context is belongs\\nto. See auditon(2) for details.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"SessionCreate\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or boolean\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.Sockets\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"This optional key is used to specify launch on demand sockets that can be used to let launchd know when\\nto run the job. The job must check-in to get a copy of the file descriptors using APIs outlined in\\nlaunch(3).  The keys of the top level Sockets dictionary can be anything. They are meant for the application\\ndeveloper to use to differentiate which descriptors correspond to which application level protocols\\n(e.g. http vs. ftp vs. DNS...).  At check-in time, the value of each Sockets dictionary key will\\nbe an array of descriptors. Daemon/Agent writers should consider all descriptors of a given key to be\\nto be effectively equivalent, even though each file descriptor likely represents a different networking\\nprotocol which conforms to the criteria specified in the job configuration file.\\n\\nThe parameters below are used as inputs to call `getaddrinfo(3)`.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"Sockets\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or (attribute set of (submodule))\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.Sockets.<name>.Bonjour\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"This optional key can be used to request that the service be registered with the\\n`mDNSResponder(8)`.  If the value is boolean, the service name is inferred from the SockServiceName.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"Sockets\",\"<name>\",\"Bonjour\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or boolean or list of string\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.Sockets.<name>.MulticastGroup\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"This optional key can be used to request that the datagram socket join a multicast group.  If the\\nvalue is a hostname, then `getaddrinfo(3)` will be used to join the correct multicast address for a\\ngiven socket family.  If an explicit IPv4 or IPv6 address is given, it is required that the SockFamily\\nfamily also be set, otherwise the results are undefined.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"Sockets\",\"<name>\",\"MulticastGroup\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or string\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.Sockets.<name>.SecureSocketWithKey\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"This optional key is a variant of SockPathName. Instead of binding to a known path, a securely\\ngenerated socket is created and the path is assigned to the environment variable that is inherited\\nby all jobs spawned by launchd.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"Sockets\",\"<name>\",\"SecureSocketWithKey\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or string\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.Sockets.<name>.SockFamily\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"This optional key can be used to specifically request that \\\"IPv4\\\" or \\\"IPv6\\\" socket(s) be created.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"Sockets\",\"<name>\",\"SockFamily\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or one of \\\"IPv4\\\", \\\"IPv6\\\"\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.Sockets.<name>.SockNodeName\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"This optional key specifies the node to `connect(2)` or `bind(2)` to.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"Sockets\",\"<name>\",\"SockNodeName\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or string\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.Sockets.<name>.SockPassive\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"This optional key specifies whether `listen(2)` or `connect(2)` should be called on the created file\\ndescriptor. The default is true (\\\"to listen\\\").\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"Sockets\",\"<name>\",\"SockPassive\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or boolean\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.Sockets.<name>.SockPathMode\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"This optional key specifies the mode of the socket. Known bug: Property lists don't support\\noctal, so please convert the value to decimal.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"Sockets\",\"<name>\",\"SockPathMode\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or signed integer\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.Sockets.<name>.SockPathName\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"This optional key implies SockFamily is set to \\\"Unix\\\". It specifies the path to `connect(2)` or\\n`bind(2)` to.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"Sockets\",\"<name>\",\"SockPathName\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or absolute path\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.Sockets.<name>.SockProtocol\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"This optional key specifies the protocol to be passed to `socket(2)`.  The only value understood by\\nthis key at the moment is \\\"TCP\\\".\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"Sockets\",\"<name>\",\"SockProtocol\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or value \\\"TCP\\\" (singular enum)\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.Sockets.<name>.SockServiceName\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"This optional key specifies the service on the node to `connect(2)` or `bind(2)` to.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"Sockets\",\"<name>\",\"SockServiceName\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or string\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.Sockets.<name>.SockType\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"This optional key tells launchctl what type of socket to create. The default is \\\"stream\\\" and\\nother valid values for this key are \\\"dgram\\\" and \\\"seqpacket\\\" respectively.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"Sockets\",\"<name>\",\"SockType\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or one of \\\"stream\\\", \\\"dgram\\\", \\\"seqpacket\\\"\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.SoftResourceLimits\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"Resource limits to be imposed on the job. These adjust variables set with `setrlimit(2)`.  The following\\nkeys apply:\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"SoftResourceLimits\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or (submodule)\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.SoftResourceLimits.CPU\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"The maximum amount of cpu time (in seconds) to be used by each process.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"SoftResourceLimits\",\"CPU\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or signed integer\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.SoftResourceLimits.Core\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"The largest size (in bytes) core file that may be created.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"SoftResourceLimits\",\"Core\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or signed integer\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.SoftResourceLimits.Data\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"The maximum size (in bytes) of the data segment for a process; this defines how far a program may\\nextend its break with the `sbrk(2)` system call.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"SoftResourceLimits\",\"Data\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or signed integer\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.SoftResourceLimits.FileSize\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"The largest size (in bytes) file that may be created.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"SoftResourceLimits\",\"FileSize\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or signed integer\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.SoftResourceLimits.MemoryLock\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"The maximum size (in bytes) which a process may lock into memory using the mlock(2) function.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"SoftResourceLimits\",\"MemoryLock\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or signed integer\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.SoftResourceLimits.NumberOfFiles\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"The maximum number of open files for this process.  Setting this value in a system wide daemon\\nwill set the `sysctl(3)` kern.maxfiles (SoftResourceLimits) or kern.maxfilesperproc (HardResourceLimits)\\nvalue in addition to the `setrlimit(2)` values.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"SoftResourceLimits\",\"NumberOfFiles\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or signed integer\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.SoftResourceLimits.NumberOfProcesses\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"The maximum number of simultaneous processes for this user id.  Setting this value in a system\\nwide daemon will set the `sysctl(3)` kern.maxproc (SoftResourceLimits) or kern.maxprocperuid\\n(HardResourceLimits) value in addition to the `setrlimit(2)` values.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"SoftResourceLimits\",\"NumberOfProcesses\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or signed integer\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.SoftResourceLimits.ResidentSetSize\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"The maximum size (in bytes) to which a process's resident set size may grow.  This imposes a\\nlimit on the amount of physical memory to be given to a process; if memory is tight, the system\\nwill prefer to take memory from processes that are exceeding their declared resident set size.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"SoftResourceLimits\",\"ResidentSetSize\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or signed integer\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.SoftResourceLimits.Stack\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"The maximum size (in bytes) of the stack segment for a process; this defines how far a program's\\nstack segment may be extended.  Stack extension is performed automatically by the system.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"SoftResourceLimits\",\"Stack\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or signed integer\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.StandardErrorPath\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"This optional key specifies what file should be used for data being sent to stderr when using `stdio(3)`.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"StandardErrorPath\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or absolute path\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.StandardInPath\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"This optional key specifies what file should be used for data being supplied to stdin when using\\n`stdio(3)`.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"StandardInPath\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or absolute path\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.StandardOutPath\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"This optional key specifies what file should be used for data being sent to stdout when using `stdio(3)`.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"StandardOutPath\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or absolute path\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.StartCalendarInterval\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"This optional key causes the job to be started every calendar interval as specified. The semantics are\\nmuch like {manpage}`crontab(5)`: Missing attributes are considered to be wildcard. Unlike cron which skips\\njob invocations when the computer is asleep, launchd will start the job the next time the computer wakes\\nup.  If multiple intervals transpire before the computer is woken, those events will be coalesced into\\none event upon waking from sleep.\\n\\n::: {.important}\\nThe list must not be empty and must not contain duplicate entries (attrsets which compare equally).\\n:::\\n\\n::: {.caution}\\nSince missing attrs become wildcards, an empty attrset effectively means \\\"every minute\\\".\\n:::\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"[\\n  {\\n    Hour = 2;\\n    Minute = 30;\\n  }\\n]\"},\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"StartCalendarInterval\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or (submodule) or unique (non-empty (list of (submodule)))\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.StartInterval\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"This optional key causes the job to be started every N seconds.  If the system is asleep, the job will\\nbe started the next time the computer wakes up.  If multiple intervals transpire before the computer is\\nwoken, those events will be coalesced into one event upon wake from sleep.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"StartInterval\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or signed integer\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.StartOnMount\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"This optional key causes the job to be started every time a filesystem is mounted.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"StartOnMount\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or boolean\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.ThrottleInterval\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"This key lets one override the default throttling policy imposed on jobs by launchd.  The value is in\\nseconds, and by default, jobs will not be spawned more than once every 10 seconds.  The principle\\nbehind this is that jobs should linger around just in case they are needed again in the near future.\\nThis not only reduces the latency of responses, but it encourages developers to amortize the cost of\\nprogram invocation.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"ThrottleInterval\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or signed integer\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.TimeOut\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"The recommended idle time out (in seconds) to pass to the job. If no value is specified, a default time\\nout will be supplied by launchd for use by the job at check in time.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"TimeOut\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or signed integer\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.Umask\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"This optional key specifies what value should be passed to `umask(2)` before running the job. Known bug:\\nProperty lists don't support octal, so please convert the value to decimal.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"Umask\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or signed integer\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.UserName\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"This optional key specifies the user to run the job as. This key is only applicable when launchd is\\nrunning as root.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"UserName\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or string\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.WaitForDebugger\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"This optional key specifies that launchd should instruct the kernel to have the job wait for a debugger\\nto attach before any code in the job is executed.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"WaitForDebugger\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or boolean\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.WatchPaths\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"This optional key causes the job to be started if any one of the listed paths are modified.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"WatchPaths\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or (list of absolute path)\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.WorkingDirectory\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"This optional key is used to specify a directory to `chdir(2)` to before running the job.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"WorkingDirectory\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or string\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.inetdCompatibility\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"The presence of this key specifies that the daemon expects to be run as if it were launched from inetd.\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"{\\n  Wait = true;\\n}\"},\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"inetdCompatibility\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or (submodule)\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.config.inetdCompatibility.Wait\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"This flag corresponds to the \\\"wait\\\" or \\\"nowait\\\" option of inetd. If true, then the listening\\nsocket is passed via the standard in/out/error file descriptors. If false, then `accept(2)` is\\ncalled on behalf of the job, and the result is passed via the standard in/out/error descriptors.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"config\",\"inetdCompatibility\",\"Wait\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or boolean or string\"},\"launchd.agents.<name>.enable\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"false\"},\"description\":\"Whether to enable ‹name›.\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"true\"},\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"agents\",\"<name>\",\"enable\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"launchd.enable\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/launchd/default.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/launchd/default.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"pkgs.stdenv.hostPlatform.isDarwin\"},\"description\":\"Whether to enable Home Manager to define per-user daemons by making use\\nof launchd's LaunchAgents.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"launchd\",\"enable\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"lib\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/misc/lib.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/misc/lib.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"{ }\"},\"description\":\"This option allows modules to define helper functions,\\nconstants, etc.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"lib\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"attribute set of (attribute set)\"},\"manual.html.enable\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/manual.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/manual.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"false\"},\"description\":\"Whether to install the HTML manual. This also installs the\\n{command}`home-manager-help` tool, which opens a local\\ncopy of the Home Manager manual in the system web browser.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"manual\",\"html\",\"enable\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"manual.json.enable\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/manual.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/manual.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"false\"},\"description\":\"Whether to install a JSON formatted list of all Home Manager\\noptions. This can be located at\\n{file}`<profile directory>/share/doc/home-manager/options.json`,\\nand may be used for navigating definitions, auto-completing,\\nand other miscellaneous tasks.\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"true\"},\"loc\":[\"manual\",\"json\",\"enable\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"manual.manpages.enable\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/manual.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/manual.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"true\"},\"description\":\"Whether to install the configuration manual page. The manual can\\nbe reached by {command}`man home-configuration.nix`.\\n\\nWhen looking at the manual page pretend that all references to\\nNixOS stuff are actually references to Home Manager stuff.\\nThanks!\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"false\"},\"loc\":[\"manual\",\"manpages\",\"enable\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"meta.maintainers\":{\"declarations\":[\"/nix/store/640irzgl08asrnjly4dspdbx8lz3cvqr-source/modules/generic/meta-maintainers.nix\"],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"[ ]\"},\"description\":\"List of maintainers of each module.\\nThis option should be defined at most once per module.\\n\\nThe option value is not a list of maintainers, but an attribute set that maps module file names to lists of maintainers.\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"[ lib.maintainers.alice lib.maintainers.bob ]\"},\"loc\":[\"meta\",\"maintainers\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"list of lib.maintainers\"},\"meta.teams\":{\"declarations\":[\"/nix/store/640irzgl08asrnjly4dspdbx8lz3cvqr-source/modules/generic/meta-maintainers.nix\"],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"[ ]\"},\"description\":\"List of team maintainers of each module.\\nThis option should be defined at most once per module.\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"[ lib.teams.acme lib.teams.haskell ]\"},\"loc\":[\"meta\",\"teams\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"list of lib.teams\"},\"news.display\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/misc/news.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/misc/news.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"\\\"notify\\\"\"},\"description\":\"How unread and relevant news should be presented when\\nrunning {command}`home-manager build` and\\n{command}`home-manager switch`.\\n\\nThe options are\\n\\n`silent`\\n: Do not print anything during build or switch. The\\n  {command}`home-manager news` command still\\n  works for viewing the entries.\\n\\n`notify`\\n: The number of unread and relevant news entries will be\\n  printed to standard output. The {command}`home-manager\\n  news` command can later be used to view the entries.\\n\\n`show`\\n: A pager showing unread news entries is opened.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"news\",\"display\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"one of \\\"silent\\\", \\\"notify\\\", \\\"show\\\"\"},\"nix.assumeXdg\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/misc/nix.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/misc/nix.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"false\"},\"description\":\"Whether Home Manager should assume that Nix is configured to use XDG\\nbase directories. Note that this doesn't change the behavior of Nix. To\\ndo that, set nix.settings.use-xdg-base-directories instead. This option\\nis intended for settings in which use-xdg-base-directories is set\\nglobally or nix.conf is unmanaged by Home Manager.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"nix\",\"assumeXdg\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"nix.buildMachines\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/misc/nix-remote-build.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/misc/nix-remote-build.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"[ ]\"},\"description\":\"This option lists the machines to be used if distributed builds are\\nenabled (see {option}`nix.distributedBuilds`).\\nNix will perform derivations on those machines via SSH by copying the\\ninputs to the Nix store on the remote machine, starting the build,\\nthen copying the output back to the local Nix store.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"nix\",\"buildMachines\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"list of (submodule)\"},\"nix.buildMachines.*.hostName\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/misc/nix-remote-build.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/misc/nix-remote-build.nix\"}],\"description\":\"The hostname of the build machine.\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"\\\"nixbuilder.example.org\\\"\"},\"loc\":[\"nix\",\"buildMachines\",\"*\",\"hostName\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"string\"},\"nix.buildMachines.*.mandatoryFeatures\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/misc/nix-remote-build.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/misc/nix-remote-build.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"[ ]\"},\"description\":\"A list of features mandatory for this builder. The builder will\\nbe ignored for derivations that don't require all features in\\nthis list. All mandatory features are automatically included in\\n{var}`supportedFeatures`.\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"[\\n  \\\"big-parallel\\\"\\n]\"},\"loc\":[\"nix\",\"buildMachines\",\"*\",\"mandatoryFeatures\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"list of string\"},\"nix.buildMachines.*.maxJobs\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/misc/nix-remote-build.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/misc/nix-remote-build.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"1\"},\"description\":\"The number of concurrent jobs the build machine supports. The\\nbuild machine will enforce its own limits, but this allows hydra\\nto schedule better since there is no work-stealing between build\\nmachines.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"nix\",\"buildMachines\",\"*\",\"maxJobs\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"signed integer\"},\"nix.buildMachines.*.protocol\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/misc/nix-remote-build.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/misc/nix-remote-build.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"\\\"ssh\\\"\"},\"description\":\"The protocol used for communicating with the build machine.\\nUse `ssh-ng` if your remote builder and your\\nlocal Nix version support that improved protocol.\\n\\nUse `null` when trying to change the special localhost builder\\nwithout a protocol which is for example used by hydra.\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"\\\"ssh-ng\\\"\"},\"loc\":[\"nix\",\"buildMachines\",\"*\",\"protocol\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"one of <null>, \\\"ssh\\\", \\\"ssh-ng\\\"\"},\"nix.buildMachines.*.publicHostKey\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/misc/nix-remote-build.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/misc/nix-remote-build.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"The (base64-encoded) public host key of this builder. The field\\nis calculated via {command}`base64 -w0 /etc/ssh/ssh_host_type_key.pub`.\\nIf null, SSH will use its regular known-hosts file when connecting.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"nix\",\"buildMachines\",\"*\",\"publicHostKey\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or string\"},\"nix.buildMachines.*.speedFactor\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/misc/nix-remote-build.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/misc/nix-remote-build.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"1\"},\"description\":\"The relative speed of this builder. This is an arbitrary integer\\nthat indicates the speed of this builder, relative to other\\nbuilders. Higher is faster.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"nix\",\"buildMachines\",\"*\",\"speedFactor\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"signed integer\"},\"nix.buildMachines.*.sshKey\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/misc/nix-remote-build.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/misc/nix-remote-build.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"The path to the SSH private key with which to authenticate on\\nthe build machine. The private key must not have a passphrase.\\nIf null, the building user (root on NixOS machines) must have an\\nappropriate ssh configuration to log in non-interactively.\\n\\nNote that for security reasons, this path must point to a file\\nin the local filesystem, *not* to the nix store.\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"\\\"/root/.ssh/id_buildhost_builduser\\\"\"},\"loc\":[\"nix\",\"buildMachines\",\"*\",\"sshKey\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or string\"},\"nix.buildMachines.*.sshUser\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/misc/nix-remote-build.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/misc/nix-remote-build.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"The username to log in as on the remote host. This user must be\\nable to log in and run nix commands non-interactively. It must\\nalso be privileged to build derivations, so must be included in\\n{option}`nix.settings.trusted-users`.\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"\\\"builder\\\"\"},\"loc\":[\"nix\",\"buildMachines\",\"*\",\"sshUser\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or string\"},\"nix.buildMachines.*.supportedFeatures\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/misc/nix-remote-build.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/misc/nix-remote-build.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"[ ]\"},\"description\":\"A list of features supported by this builder. The builder will\\nbe ignored for derivations that require features not in this\\nlist.\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"[\\n  \\\"kvm\\\"\\n  \\\"big-parallel\\\"\\n]\"},\"loc\":[\"nix\",\"buildMachines\",\"*\",\"supportedFeatures\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"list of string\"},\"nix.buildMachines.*.systems\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/misc/nix-remote-build.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/misc/nix-remote-build.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"[ ]\"},\"description\":\"The system types the build machine can execute derivations on.\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"[\\n  \\\"x86_64-linux\\\"\\n  \\\"aarch64-linux\\\"\\n]\"},\"loc\":[\"nix\",\"buildMachines\",\"*\",\"systems\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"list of string\"},\"nix.channels\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/misc/nix.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/misc/nix.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"{ }\"},\"description\":\"A declarative alternative to Nix channels. Whereas with stock channels,\\nyou would register URLs and fetch them into the Nix store with\\n{manpage}`nix-channel(1)`, this option allows you to register the store\\npath directly. One particularly useful example is registering flake\\ninputs as channels.\\n\\nThis option can coexist with stock Nix channels. If the same channel is\\ndefined in both, this option takes precedence.\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"{ inherit nixpkgs; }\"},\"loc\":[\"nix\",\"channels\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"attribute set of package\"},\"nix.checkConfig\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/misc/nix.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/misc/nix.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"true\"},\"description\":\"If enabled (the default), checks for data type mismatches and that Nix\\ncan parse the generated nix.conf.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"nix\",\"checkConfig\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"nix.distributedBuilds\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/misc/nix-remote-build.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/misc/nix-remote-build.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"false\"},\"description\":\"Whether to distribute builds to the machines listed in\\n{option}`nix.buildMachines`.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"nix\",\"distributedBuilds\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"nix.extraOptions\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/misc/nix.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/misc/nix.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"\\\"\\\"\"},\"description\":\"Additional text appended to {file}`nix.conf`.\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"''\\n  keep-outputs = true\\n  keep-derivations = true\\n''\"},\"loc\":[\"nix\",\"extraOptions\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"strings concatenated with \\\"\\\\n\\\"\"},\"nix.gc.automatic\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/services/nix-gc.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/services/nix-gc.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"false\"},\"description\":\"Automatically run the garbage collector at a specific time.\\n\\nNote: This will only garbage collect the current user's profiles.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"nix\",\"gc\",\"automatic\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"nix.gc.dates\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/services/nix-gc.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/services/nix-gc.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"\\\"weekly\\\"\"},\"description\":\"When to run the Nix garbage collector.\\n\\nOn Linux this is a string as defined by {manpage}`systemd.time(7)`.\\n\\nOn Darwin, it must be one of: hourly, daily, weekly, monthly, semiannually, annually, which are implemented as defined in {manpage}`systemd.time(7)`.\\n\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"\\\"03:15\\\"\"},\"loc\":[\"nix\",\"gc\",\"dates\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"(optionally newline-terminated) single-line string or list of string\"},\"nix.gc.options\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/services/nix-gc.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/services/nix-gc.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"Options given to {file}`nix-collect-garbage` when the\\ngarbage collector is run automatically.\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"\\\"--max-freed $((64 * 1024**3))\\\"\"},\"loc\":[\"nix\",\"gc\",\"options\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or string\"},\"nix.gc.persistent\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/services/nix-gc.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/services/nix-gc.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"true\"},\"description\":\"If true, the time when the service unit was last triggered is\\nstored on disk. When the timer is activated, the service unit is\\ntriggered immediately if it would have been triggered at least once\\nduring the time when the timer was inactive.\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"false\"},\"loc\":[\"nix\",\"gc\",\"persistent\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"nix.gc.randomizedDelaySec\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/services/nix-gc.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/services/nix-gc.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"\\\"0\\\"\"},\"description\":\"Add a randomized delay before each garbage collection.\\nThe delay will be chosen between zero and this value.\\nThis value must be a time span in the format specified by\\n{manpage}`systemd.time(7)`\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"\\\"45min\\\"\"},\"loc\":[\"nix\",\"gc\",\"randomizedDelaySec\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"(optionally newline-terminated) single-line string\"},\"nix.keepOldNixPath\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/misc/nix.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/misc/nix.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"true\"},\"description\":\"Whether {option}`nix.nixPath` should keep the previously set values in\\n{env}`NIX_PATH`.\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"false\"},\"loc\":[\"nix\",\"keepOldNixPath\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"nix.nixPath\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/misc/nix.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/misc/nix.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"[ ]\"},\"description\":\"Adds new directories to the Nix expression search path.\\n\\nUsed by Nix when looking up paths in angular brackets\\n(e.g. `<nixpkgs>`).\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"[\\n  \\\"$HOME/.nix-defexpr/channels\\\"\\n  \\\"darwin-config=$HOME/.config/nixpkgs/darwin-configuration.nix\\\"\\n]\"},\"loc\":[\"nix\",\"nixPath\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"list of string\"},\"nix.package\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/misc/nix.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/misc/nix.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"The nix package to use.\",\"loc\":[\"nix\",\"package\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or package\"},\"nix.registry\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/misc/nix.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/misc/nix.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"{ }\"},\"description\":\"User level flake registry.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"nix\",\"registry\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"attribute set of (submodule)\"},\"nix.registry.<name>.exact\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/misc/nix.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/misc/nix.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"true\"},\"description\":\"Whether the {option}`from` reference needs to match exactly. If set,\\na {option}`from` reference like `nixpkgs` does not\\nmatch with a reference like `nixpkgs/nixos-20.03`.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"nix\",\"registry\",\"<name>\",\"exact\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"nix.registry.<name>.flake\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/misc/nix.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/misc/nix.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"The flake input to which {option}`from>` is to be rewritten.\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"nixpkgs\"},\"loc\":[\"nix\",\"registry\",\"<name>\",\"flake\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or (attribute set)\"},\"nix.registry.<name>.from\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/misc/nix.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/misc/nix.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"{ }\"},\"description\":\"The flake reference to be rewritten.\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"{\\n  id = \\\"nixpkgs\\\";\\n  type = \\\"indirect\\\";\\n}\"},\"loc\":[\"nix\",\"registry\",\"<name>\",\"from\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"attribute set of (string or signed integer or boolean or package)\"},\"nix.registry.<name>.to\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/misc/nix.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/misc/nix.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"{ }\"},\"description\":\"The flake reference to which {option}`from>` is to be rewritten.\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"{\\n  owner = \\\"my-org\\\";\\n  repo = \\\"my-nixpkgs\\\";\\n  type = \\\"github\\\";\\n}\"},\"loc\":[\"nix\",\"registry\",\"<name>\",\"to\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"attribute set of (string or signed integer or boolean or package)\"},\"nix.settings\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/misc/nix.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/misc/nix.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"{ }\"},\"description\":\"Configuration for Nix; see {manpage}`nix.conf(5)` for available options.\\nThe value declared here will be translated directly to the key-value pairs Nix expects.\\n\\nConfiguration specified in [](#opt-nix.extraOptions) will be appended\\nverbatim to the resulting config file.\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"{\\n  sandbox = true;\\n  show-trace = true;\\n  system-features = [\\n    \\\"big-parallel\\\"\\n    \\\"kvm\\\"\\n    \\\"recursive-nix\\\"\\n  ];\\n}\"},\"loc\":[\"nix\",\"settings\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"open submodule of attribute set of (Nix config atom (null, bool, int, float, str, path or package) or list of (Nix config atom (null, bool, int, float, str, path or package)))\"},\"nixpkgs.config\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/misc/nixpkgs.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/misc/nixpkgs.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"The configuration of the Nix Packages collection. (For\\ndetails, see the Nixpkgs documentation.) It allows you to set\\npackage configuration options.\\n\\nIf `null`, then configuration is taken from\\nthe fallback location, for example,\\n{file}`~/.config/nixpkgs/config.nix`.\\n\\nNote, this option will not apply outside your Home Manager\\nconfiguration like when installing manually through\\n{command}`nix-env`. If you want to apply it both\\ninside and outside Home Manager you can put it in a separate\\nfile and include something like\\n\\n```nix\\n  nixpkgs.config = import ./nixpkgs-config.nix;\\n  xdg.configFile.\\\"nixpkgs/config.nix\\\".source = ./nixpkgs-config.nix;\\n```\\n\\nin your Home Manager configuration.\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"{\\n  allowBroken = true;\\n}\"},\"loc\":[\"nixpkgs\",\"config\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or (nixpkgs config)\"},\"nixpkgs.overlays\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/misc/nixpkgs.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/misc/nixpkgs.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"null\"},\"description\":\"List of overlays to use with the Nix Packages collection. (For\\ndetails, see the Nixpkgs documentation.) It allows you to\\noverride packages globally. This is a function that takes as\\nan argument the *original* Nixpkgs. The\\nfirst argument should be used for finding dependencies, and\\nthe second should be used for overriding recipes.\\n\\nIf `null`, then the overlays are taken from\\nthe fallback location, for example,\\n{file}`~/.config/nixpkgs/overlays`.\\n\\nLike {var}`nixpkgs.config` this option only\\napplies within the Home Manager configuration. See\\n{var}`nixpkgs.config` for a suggested setup that\\nworks both internally and externally.\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"[\\n  (final: prev: {\\n    openssh = prev.openssh.override {\\n      hpnSupport = true;\\n      withKerberos = true;\\n      kerberos = final.libkrb5;\\n    };\\n  })\\n]\\n\"},\"loc\":[\"nixpkgs\",\"overlays\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or (list of (nixpkgs overlay))\"},\"pam.sessionVariables\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/misc/pam.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/misc/pam.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"{ }\"},\"description\":\"Environment variables that will be set for the PAM session.\\nThe variable values must be as described in\\n{manpage}`pam_env.conf(5)`.\\n\\nNote, this option will become deprecated in the future and its use is\\ntherefore discouraged.\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"{\\n  EDITOR = \\\"vim\\\";\\n}\"},\"loc\":[\"pam\",\"sessionVariables\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"attribute set\"},\"pam.yubico.authorizedYubiKeys.ids\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/misc/pam.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/misc/pam.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"[ ]\"},\"description\":\"List of authorized YubiKey token IDs. Refer to\\n<https://developers.yubico.com/yubico-pam>\\nfor details on how to obtain the token ID of a YubiKey.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"pam\",\"yubico\",\"authorizedYubiKeys\",\"ids\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"list of string of length 12\"},\"pam.yubico.authorizedYubiKeys.path\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/misc/pam.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/misc/pam.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"\\\".yubico/authorized_yubikeys\\\"\"},\"description\":\"File path to write the authorized YubiKeys,\\nrelative to {env}`HOME`.\\n\",\"loc\":[\"pam\",\"yubico\",\"authorizedYubiKeys\",\"path\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"string\"},\"programs.abaddon.enable\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/programs/abaddon.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/programs/abaddon.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"false\"},\"description\":\"Whether to enable abaddon.\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"true\"},\"loc\":[\"programs\",\"abaddon\",\"enable\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"programs.abaddon.package\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/programs/abaddon.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/programs/abaddon.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"pkgs.abaddon\"},\"description\":\"The abaddon package to use.\",\"loc\":[\"programs\",\"abaddon\",\"package\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or package\"},\"programs.abaddon.settings\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/programs/abaddon.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/programs/abaddon.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"{ }\"},\"description\":\"Configuration settings for abaddon. All the available options can be found here:\\n<https://github.com/uowuo/abaddon?tab=readme-ov-file#settings>\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"{\\n  discord = {\\n    autoconnect = true;\\n    token = \\\"MZ1yGvKTjE0rY0cV8i47CjAa.uRHQPq.Xb1Mk2nEhe-4iUcrGOuegj57zMC\\\";\\n  };\\n  gui = {\\n    alt_menu = true;\\n    animations = false;\\n    hide_to_tray = true;\\n    stock_emojis = false;\\n  };\\n  notifications = {\\n    enabled = false;\\n  };\\n  windows = {\\n    hideconsole = true;\\n  };\\n}\"},\"loc\":[\"programs\",\"abaddon\",\"settings\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"attribute set of section of an INI file (attrs of INI atom (null, bool, int, float or string))\"},\"programs.abook.enable\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/programs/abook.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/programs/abook.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"false\"},\"description\":\"Whether to enable Abook.\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"true\"},\"loc\":[\"programs\",\"abook\",\"enable\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"programs.abook.extraConfig\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/programs/abook.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/programs/abook.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"\\\"\\\"\"},\"description\":\"Extra lines added to {file}`$HOME/.config/abook/abookrc`.\\nAvailable configuration options are described in the abook repository:\\n<https://sourceforge.net/p/abook/git/ci/master/tree/sample.abookrc>.\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"''\\n  field pager = Pager\\n  view CONTACT = name, email\\n  set autosave=true\\n''\"},\"loc\":[\"programs\",\"abook\",\"extraConfig\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"strings concatenated with \\\"\\\\n\\\"\"},\"programs.abook.package\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/programs/abook.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/programs/abook.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"pkgs.abook\"},\"description\":\"The abook package to use.\",\"loc\":[\"programs\",\"abook\",\"package\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"null or package\"},\"programs.acd-cli.cacheSettings\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/programs/acd-cli.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/programs/acd-cli.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"{ }\"},\"description\":\"Cache configuration settings for acd-cli. All the available options can be found here:\\n<https://acd-cli.readthedocs.io/en/latest/configuration.html#cache-ini>.\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"{\\n  blacklist = {\\n    folders = [ ];\\n  };\\n  sqlite = {\\n    busy_timeout = 30000;\\n    filename = \\\"nodes.db\\\";\\n    journal_mode = \\\"wal\\\";\\n  };\\n}\"},\"loc\":[\"programs\",\"acd-cli\",\"cacheSettings\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"attribute set of section of an INI file (attrs of INI atom (null, bool, int, float or string))\"},\"programs.acd-cli.cliSettings\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/programs/acd-cli.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/programs/acd-cli.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"{ }\"},\"description\":\"CLI configuration settings for acd-cli. All the available options can be found here:\\n<https://acd-cli.readthedocs.io/en/latest/configuration.html#acd-cli-ini>.\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"{\\n  download = {\\n    keep_corrupt = false;\\n    keep_incomplete = true;\\n  };\\n  upload = {\\n    timeout_wait = 10;\\n  };\\n}\"},\"loc\":[\"programs\",\"acd-cli\",\"cliSettings\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"attribute set of section of an INI file (attrs of INI atom (null, bool, int, float or string))\"},\"programs.acd-cli.clientSettings\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/programs/acd-cli.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/programs/acd-cli.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"{ }\"},\"description\":\"Client configuration settings for acd-cli. All the available options can be found here:\\n<https://acd-cli.readthedocs.io/en/latest/configuration.html#acd-client-ini>.\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"{\\n  endpoints = {\\n    filename = \\\"endpoint_data\\\";\\n    validity_duration = 259200;\\n  };\\n  transfer = {\\n    chunk_retries = 1;\\n    connection_timeout = 30;\\n    dl_chunk_size = 524288000;\\n    fs_chunk_size = 131072;\\n    idle_timeout = 60;\\n  };\\n}\"},\"loc\":[\"programs\",\"acd-cli\",\"clientSettings\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"attribute set of section of an INI file (attrs of INI atom (null, bool, int, float or string))\"},\"programs.acd-cli.enable\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/programs/acd-cli.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/programs/acd-cli.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"false\"},\"description\":\"Whether to enable acd-cli.\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"true\"},\"loc\":[\"programs\",\"acd-cli\",\"enable\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"programs.acd-cli.fuseSettings\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/programs/acd-cli.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/release-26.05/modules/programs/acd-cli.nix\"}],\"default\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"{ }\"},\"description\":\"FUSE configuration settings for acd-cli. All the available options can be found here:\\n<https://acd-cli.readthedocs.io/en/latest/configuration.html#fuse-ini>.\\n\",\"example\":{\"_type\":\"literalExpression\",\"text\":\"{\\n  fs = {\\n    block_size = 512;\\n  };\\n  read = {\\n    open_chunk_limit = 10;\\n  };\\n  write = {\\n    buffer_size = 32;\\n    timeout = 30;\\n  };\\n}\"},\"loc\":[\"programs\",\"acd-cli\",\"fuseSettings\"],\"readOnly\":false,\"type\":\"attribute set of section of an INI file (attrs of INI atom (null, bool, int, float or string))\"},\"programs.acd-cli.package\":{\"declarations\":[{\"name\":\"<home-manager/modules/programs/acd-cli.nix>\",\"url\":\"https://gi